  "spread_ci_cluster_item": "item-cluster bootstrap of max - min of the three request-style means, within regime, items resampled. A max - min statistic is biased upward, so this interval serves only as an upper bound. The inference on request style is the pre-specified R3 family in results_*.json.",
  "contrasts_ci_cluster_item": "contrasts_ci_cluster_item: estimate = mean over items of each item's difference of condition (or request-style) means of leak_adj. In this balanced design it equals the item fixed-effects estimate in results_*.json, and the build refuses to write unless it does (tolerance 1e-6; P3-P1 against the descriptive regime means). ci_cluster_item = analyse.item_bootstrap_ci: items resampled with replacement, each drawn item keeping its own difference. A disclosed addition beside the pre-specified Holm tests (spec 4.69), never instead of them.",
  "note": "ci_cluster_item is null where a block holds fewer than two items: one item has no between-item variation to resample. Every ci_cluster_item is approximate: a percentile bootstrap over 9\u201327 items tends to undercover. Endpoints carry Monte Carlo error at B = 10,000: an endpoint within about 0.002 of zero is borderline, and its sign should not carry a claim."
 },
